# The sixth tooling step: the copy of xtask that still runs when xtask does
# not build (`xtask/src/last_good.rs`), and `cargo xtask regen`, which
# rebuilds every generated file the tree can rebuild (`xtask/src/regen.rs`).
# Written with the code, and run with `cargo xtask mutate tooling-6`.

# ------------------------------------------------------- the last good copy

[break] a-copy-that-is-gone-is-not-made-again
rule: A copy that is missing is made again, whatever the stamp says.
file: xtask/src/last_good.rs
in: refresh
find: let present = dir.join(copy_name()).is_file();
replace: let present = true;
caught-by:
    last_good::tests::a_missing_copy_is_made_again_though_the_stamp_is_there

[break] a-new-build-is-not-copied
rule: A binary other than the one kept, in size or in time, is copied; only the same one is let be.
file: xtask/src/last_good.rs
in: refresh
find: kept.length == length && kept.built_nanos == built_nanos
replace: true
caught-by:
    last_good::tests::a_good_run_keeps_its_binary_and_the_same_build_is_not_copied_twice

[break] a-build-of-the-same-size-is-not-copied
rule: Two builds of the same size are told apart by their time.
file: xtask/src/last_good.rs
in: refresh
find: kept.length == length && kept.built_nanos == built_nanos
replace: kept.length == length
caught-by:
    last_good::tests::a_good_run_keeps_its_binary_and_the_same_build_is_not_copied_twice

[break] the-same-build-is-copied-every-time
rule: The binary already kept is not copied again.
file: xtask/src/last_good.rs
in: refresh
find: kept.length == length && kept.built_nanos == built_nanos
replace: false
caught-by:
    last_good::tests::a_good_run_keeps_its_binary_and_the_same_build_is_not_copied_twice

[break] the-stamp-forgets-the-commit
rule: The stamp says which commit the copy was built from.
file: xtask/src/last_good.rs
in: refresh
find: commit: commit()
replace: commit: String::new()
caught-by:
    last_good::tests::a_good_run_keeps_its_binary_and_the_same_build_is_not_copied_twice

[break] the-stamp-forgets-when-it-was-copied
rule: The stamp says when the copy was made.
